hub.com/repos/yewstack/yew/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yewstack/yew/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yewstack/yew/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yewstack/yew/deployments","created_at":"2017-12-16T14:19:02Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T19:55:30Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T03:08:10Z","git_url":"git://github.com/yewstack/yew.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:yewstack/yew.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/yewstack/yew.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/yewstack/yew","homepage":"https://yew.rs","size":17267,"stargazers_count":32201,"watchers_count":32201,"language":"Rust","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":1455,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":155,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["asmjs","concurrency","elm","emscripten","gui","hacktoberfest","jsx","multithreading","rust","wasm","web","web-framework","webworkers"],"visibility":"public","forks":1455,"open_issues":155,"watchers":32201,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"**Problem**\r\n<!-- A clear and concise description of what the bug is. -->\r\n\r\nI spent a long time on this last night - still not quite sure what's happening. This might be because of #948 - but regardless, there's no `register` implementation for `private` because `private` does not implement `threaded`. When spawning a Private agent, nothing happens so (I'm assuming) the agent is released. But! if I compile it as a public worker, move the wasm/js into static, I can actually create the worker. I know it's being handled as a private worker because I can spawn a few dozen of the same (something I haven't been able to with public workers yet). My workaround is okay for now, but bad for CI/build.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Environment:**\r\n - Yew version v14.1\r\n - Rust version 1.42.0\r\n - Target if relevant `wasm32-unknown-unknown`\r\n- `stdweb` though I can get it working with web-sys\r\n- macos\r\n - Firefox 74 + Safari\r\n\r\n**Questionnaire**\r\n<!-- Developing Yew is a community effort! -->\r\n<!-- If you feel up to the challenge, please check one of the boxes below: -->\r\n- [x] I'm interested in fixing this myself but don't know where to start\r\n- [x] I would like to fix and I have a solution\r\n- [ ] I don't have time to fix this right now, but maybe later\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yewstack/yew/issues/1046/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yewstack/yew/issues/1046/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"jstarry","id":1076145,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzYxNDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1076145?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jstarry","html_url":"https://github.com/jstarry","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jstarry/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jstarry/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jstarry/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jstarry/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jstarry/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jstarry/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jstarry/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jstarry/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jstarry/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type